    "type": "question",
    "label": "21",
    "prompt": "Prove that ${}^{n+1}P_r = {}^{n}P_r + r \\times {}^{n}P_{r-1}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$${}^{n}P_r+r\\times{}^{n}P_{r-1}=\\frac{(n+1)!}{(n+1-r)!}={}^{n+1}P_r.$$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&={}^{n+1}P_r=\\frac{(n+1)!}{(n+1-r)!}.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{RHS}&={}^{n}P_r+r\\times{}^{n}P_{r-1}\\\\&=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}+r\\times\\frac{n!}{(n-r+1)!}\\\\&=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}+r\\times\\frac{n!}{(n-r+1)(n-r)!}\\\\&=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\times\\left[1+\\frac{r}{n-r+1}\\right]\\\\&=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\times\\left[\\frac{n-r+1+r}{n-r+1}\\right]\\\\&=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\times\\frac{n+1}{n+1-r}\\\\&=(n+1)\\times\\frac{n!}{(n+1-r)!}\\\\&=\\frac{(n+1)!}{(n+1-r)!}\\\\&=\\mathrm{LHS}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
